{
  "dom_id": "step-q126260",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226762/assets/38e504d9538d35b8fbee3e38973205172ef7fc0e54f68c2a4fdeb6feb5b340eb.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the area of the shaded region that lies between the polar curves $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ and $r=\\sqrt{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ as shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the values of $\\theta $ for which the two curves intersect:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\sqrt{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have two solutions: \n\n$\\,$ $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$    \n\nTo determine the inner function and the outer, let's draw an arrow from the origin that passes through the shaded region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226762/assets/1a99df490145fae473eb72c320bb4971fe10b63e1a6f15a4fb8c699f01fb6f83.png)\n\nThe arrow\n\n- *enters* the region through the inner function $r=\\sqrt{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the outer function $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTo find the area, we use the formula\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}([\\text{outer}]^{2}-[\\text{inner}]^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere\n\n$\\,$ ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,$ and $\\,{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$    \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}((3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}-(\\sqrt{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -(2+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(8{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2)\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
      "type": "radio",
